<title>UK: Lloyds details berthing delays at S.Korean ports.</title>
<headline>Lloyds details berthing delays at S.Korean ports.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lloyds casualty  reported the following berthing delays at South Korean ports.</p>
<p>At Busan 153 vessels were in port, 62 at berth and 91 at anchorage. Berthing delays of around two to three days were reported.</p>
<p>Ulsan had 110 vessels in port of which 70 were at berth and 40 at anchorage berthing delays are usually around one to two days, Lloyds said.</p>
<p>At Pohang 31 vessels were in port, 27 at berth and four at anchorage, no delays were reported.</p>
<p>Inchon had 67 vessels in port, 49 at berth and 18 at anchorage. Berthing delays usually of around one to two days were reported.</p>
<p>--Colin Wooster, London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7456</p>
